% MBB beam topology — a library example (run it with F5; "Make a copy" to change it)
%
% The classic test of topology optimization: a simply supported beam with a load at mid-span, of which top88
% models the left half (60 × 20 elements, symmetry on the left edge, a roller under the bottom-right corner, the
% load down at the top-left). It keeps half the material (volfrac 0.5) where it makes the beam stiffest. Watch the
% densities form (the image in the dock), the compliance fall (the plot), and the final design on the canvas.
% Try ft = 2 (density filter), a smaller rmin for finer members, or nelx = 120, nely = 40 (slower).
% Expected: 94 iterations, compliance 203.19 (Andreassen et al. 2011, the published code).
clf                                    % start with an empty canvas and dock
nelx = 60; nely = 20; volfrac = 0.5; penal = 3; rmin = 1.5; ft = 1;
[x, c, loop, hist] = top88(nelx, nely, volfrac, penal, rmin, ft);
fprintf('top88: %d iterations, compliance %.4f, volume %.3f\n', loop, c, mean(x(:)));
